   :db/valueType   :db.type/keyword
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
   :db/doc "Hook lifecycle position — when in the Claude Code lifecycle this hook-event class fires.  Values: :pre-grounding, :pre-tool-use, :post-commit, :post-response, :session-start, :session-end, :user-prompt-submit, :corpus-audit, etc.  Migrated from the legacy :mm.event/lifecycle-position slot per the 2026-05-24 collision-resolution ADR."}

  {:db/ident       :mm.hook-event/default-severity
   :dt/type        :dt/Property
   :dt/domain      :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/range       :db.type/keyword
   :db/valueType   :db.type/keyword
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
   :db/doc "Default severity for rules triggered by this hook-event class.  Values: :audit (informational), :warn (advisory), :block (enforcement).  Migrated from legacy :mm.event/default-severity."}

  {:db/ident       :mm.hook-event/triggered-by-hook
   :dt/type        :dt/Property
   :dt/domain      :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/range       :db.type/string
   :db/valueType   :db.type/string
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
   :db/doc "Path to the hook script that fires this hook-event class (e.g., 'hooks/session_start.sh') OR special-form keyword like ':user-prompt' / ':session-init'.  Migrated from legacy :mm.event/triggered-by-hook."}

  {:db/ident       :mm.hook-event/applicable-actor-classes
   :dt/type        :dt/Property
   :dt/domain      :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/range       :mm/Actor
   :db/valueType   :db.type/ref
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
   :db/doc "Actor classes for which rules triggered by this hook-event class apply.  Migrated from legacy :mm.event/applicable-actor-classes."}

  {:db/ident       :mm.hook-event/substrate-correctness-criticality
   :dt/type        :dt/Property
   :dt/domain      :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/range       :db.type/keyword
   :db/valueType   :db.type/keyword
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
   :db/doc "Substrate-correctness tier classification.  Values: :tier-0 (foundational; substrate breaks without rules at this event), :tier-1 (substrate-critical), :tier-2 (operationally-important), :tier-3 (advisory).  Migrated from legacy :mm.event/substrate-correctness-criticality."}]


;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; Class definitions — 6 new classes
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

 [{:db/ident         :mm/Spec
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Memory
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Spec"
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract root of the DECLARATIVE family — recipe / pattern / type-of-action / how-to.  Per Phase 2 type-lattice ADR D.1 + D.2.  Concrete subtypes: :mm/Workflow (existing; additively re-parented), :mm/Fn (existing; additively re-parented), :mm/Job (new), :mm/Schedule (new), :mm/EffectSpec (new abstract sub-root).  Specs are TIMELESS + REUSABLE — a Spec can be executed many times; each execution produces an :mm/Activity instance referencing its Spec via :mm.activity/spec."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Process
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Activity
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Process"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.process/workflow :mm.process/state :mm.process/runs]
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract supertype of :workflow/Process — multi-step running instance of a :mm/Workflow.  Per Phase 2 ADR D.3.  :workflow/Process becomes a subclass additively via the re-parenting at the end of this file.  Composes with the existing workflow-substrate state-machine via :mm.process/state."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Job
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Job"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.job/fn :mm.job/payload-shape :mm.job/effect-spec]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Single-step Spec specifying an action to invoke.  Per Phase 2 ADR D.2.  Re-target from the legacy :job/{Scheduled, Recurring, Task, Triggered} family via the Phase 3 migration tx-fn (sandbar.scripts.migrate-mm-temporal).  Each :mm/Job firing produces a :mm/Run referencing it via :mm.run/job."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Schedule
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Schedule"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.schedule/target :mm.schedule/recurrence :mm.schedule/timezone
                      :mm.schedule/dtstart :mm.schedule/until :mm.schedule/count
                      :mm.schedule/rdates :mm.schedule/exdates
                      :mm.schedule/source-nl :mm.schedule/source-cron
                      :mm.schedule/next-fire-at
                      :mm.schedule/misfire-policy :mm.schedule/concurrency]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Recurrence Spec firing a :mm/Workflow or :mm/Job per its target.  OWL-Time + RFC 5545 RRULE aligned per the temporal-substrate arc plan §1.1+§1.2.  Each firing produces a new :mm/Process (target=Workflow) or :mm/Run (target=Job).  Per Phase 2 ADR D.2 + D.8."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/EffectSpec
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "EffectSpec"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.effect/initiates :mm.effect/terminates
                      :mm.effect/preserves :mm.effect/preconditions]
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract Spec subtype encoding Reiter-style successor-state axioms as DATA, SHACL-validatable at execution time.  Frame-problem-aware per Phase 2 ADR D.4 (Cyc agent finding: the frame problem WILL bite Sandbar in workflow-step form).  When a :mm/Run of a :mm/Job carrying an EffectSpec completes, sandbar can VALIDATE that the actual tx-data conformed to the declared :mm.effect/{initiates, terminates, preserves} sets + that :mm.effect/preconditions held."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Event
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "HookEvent"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.hook-event/lifecycle-position :mm.hook-event/default-severity
                      :mm.hook-event/triggered-by-hook
                      :mm.hook-event/applicable-actor-classes
                      :mm.hook-event/substrate-correctness-criticality]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Concrete subtype of :mm/Event capturing the corpus-hook event taxonomy authored 2026-05-11 (per decisions/event_as_first_class_type_2026_05_11.md).  Receives the 6 existing :mm/Event instances (:memory.events/{session_start, post_commit, pre_grounding, corpus_audit, pre_tool_use, user_prompt_submit}) via the 2026-05-24 collision-resolution migration tx-fn.  Carries :mm.hook-event/* slots (renamed from the legacy :mm.event/{lifecycle-position,default-severity,...} family).  Rules continue to reference instances of this class via :triggered-by typed edges (no rule-side migration needed; only :dt/type of the referenced instances changes from :mm/Event to :mm/HookEvent)."}]


;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; Additive re-parenting — adds :dt/subclass-of edges WITHOUT retracting existing
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; :dt/subclass-of is :db.cardinality/many — adding a new parent does NOT
;; retract existing parentage.  Per Phase 2 ADR §2 + collision-resolution ADR §2.
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

 [;; :mm/Workflow + :mm/Fn — add :mm/Spec parent (preserves :mm/Meta parent)
  {:db/ident :mm/Workflow      :dt/subclass-of :mm/Spec}
  {:db/ident :mm/Fn            :dt/subclass-of :mm/Spec}

  ;; :workflow/Process — add :mm/Process parent (preserves :dt/Ref parent)
  {:db/ident :workflow/Process :dt/subclass-of :mm/Process}

  ;; :event/* family — add :mm/Event parent (preserves :dt/Event parent for back-compat)
  {:db/ident :event/SystemEvent :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}
  {:db/ident :event/ApiCall     :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}
  {:db/ident :event/HttpRequest :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}
  {:db/ident :event/Transaction :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}
  {:db/ident :event/ServerEvent :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}
  {:db/ident :event/UserEvent   :dt/subclass-of :mm/Event}]

]
